:{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["bevy","game-development","game-engine","gamedev","open-source","rust"],"visibility":"public","forks":4270,"open_issues":3179,"watchers":43454,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"**Bevy version**\r\n\r\nBevy 0.4\r\n\r\n**Operating system & version**\r\n\r\nWindows 10\r\n\r\n**What you did**\r\n\r\nCreate a `TextureAtlas` sprite that is a single pixel in size, attempt to draw that with a `SpriteSheetBundle` at a location.\r\n\r\n**What you expected to happen**\r\n\r\nThe single pixel should be drawn with it's center at the location.\r\n\r\n**What actually happened**\r\n\r\nThe single pixel is drawn shifted up 0.5 and right 0.5.\r\n\r\n**Additional information**\r\n\r\nThis is a file that produces the problem. In the `assets` directory in the usual place, there is a file called \"one.png\". I've attached it here, but it's only one pixel so it's very small. Any one-pixel image should work.\r\n![\"one.png\"](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/20546688/107262747-ed677980-6a0e-11eb-97c4-4409abed5972.png).\r\n\r\n```rust\r\nuse bevy::prelude::*;\r\n\r\nfn main()\r\n{\r\n    App::build()\r\n        .add_plugins(DefaultPlugins)\r\n        .add_startup_system(startup.system())\r\n        .run();\r\n}\r\n\r\nfn startup(\r\n    server: Res<AssetServer>,\r\n    mut atlases: ResMut<Assets<TextureAtlas>>,\r\n    mut materials: ResMut<Assets<ColorMaterial>>,\r\n    commands: &mut Commands)\r\n{\r\n    let handle = server.load(\"one.png\");\r\n\r\n    let atlas = atlases.add(TextureAtlas::from_grid(\r\n        handle.clone(),\r\n        Vec2::new(1.0, 1.0),\r\n        1,\r\n        1));\r\n\r\n    let material = materials.add(ColorMaterial::color(Color::BLACK));\r\n\r\n    let mut camera_transform = Transform::default();\r\n    // zoomed to show the single pixel better\r\n    camera_transform.scale = Vec3::new(1.0 / 500.0, 1.0 / 500.0, 1.0);\r\n    camera_transform.translation = Vec3::new(0.0, 0.0, 1.0);\r\n\r\n    commands\r\n        .spawn(Camera2dBundle\r\n        {\r\n            transform: camera_transform,\r\n            orthographic_projection: bevy::render::camera::OrthographicProjection\r\n            {\r\n                // needed for scales < 1\r\n                far: 1000.0 / (1.0 / 500.0),\r\n                ..Default::default()\r\n            },\r\n            ..Default::default()\r\n        })\r\n        .spawn(SpriteSheetBundle\r\n        {\r\n            sprite: TextureAtlasSprite\r\n            {\r\n                index: 0,\r\n                ..Default::default()\r\n            },\r\n            texture_atlas: atlas,\r\n            transform: Transform::from_translation(Vec3::new(\r\n                0.0,\r\n                0.0,\r\n                0.0)),\r\n            ..Default::default()\r\n        })\r\n        .spawn(SpriteBundle\r\n        {\r\n            sprite: Sprite::new(Vec2::new(1.0, 1.0)),\r\n            material: material.clone(),\r\n            transform: Transform::from_translation(Vec3::new(\r\n                0.0,\r\n                0.0,\r\n                1.0,)),\r\n            ..Default::default()\r\n        });\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere is a screenshot of the behaviour, the blue pixel is from the `TextureAtlas`, the black pixel is a simple `ColorMaterial` sprite, both have the same `Transform`s.\r\n![wrong](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/20546688/107263002-391a2300-6a0f-11eb-9717-9e5ee3af028a.png)\r\n\r\nIf you alter the `SpriteSheetBundle`'s `transform` property to be\r\n\r\n```rust\r\n            transform: Transform::from_translation(Vec3::new(\r\n                -0.5,\r\n                -0.5,\r\n                0.0)),\r\n```\r\n\r\nthen you get this screenshot:\r\n![right](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/20546688/107263396-ad54c680-6a0f-11eb-8a93-990dc6f6b16c.png)\r\n\r\nAs you can see, the black pixel completely covers the blue pixel, even though they're supposedly offset by `(-0.5, -0.5)`\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/1421/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/1421/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":4338791125,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDQzMzg3OTExMjU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/events/4338791125","actor":{"login":"alice-i-cecile","id":3579909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1Nzk5MDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3579909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alice-i-cecile","html_url":"https://github.com/alice-i-cecile","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alice-i-cecile/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alice-i-cecile/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alice-i-cecile/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alice-i-cecile/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alice-i-cecile/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alice-i-cecile/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alice-i-cecile/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alice-i-cecile/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alice-i-cecile/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2021-02-16T23:58:39Z","label":{"name":"bug","color":"d73a4a"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":4338791695,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDQzMzg3OTE2OTU=","url":"https://api